# Root .dockerignore — applies to the backend image build (backend/Dockerfile
# is built with the repo root as context; see that file's top comment).
# Keeps the build context small and out of the daemon's upload entirely
# rather than merely unused: secrets/tests/other packages' node_modules never
# leave the host.

# Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image via `npm ci`/`pip install`).
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# VCS / CI.
.git
.github

# The Expo mobile app is not part of the backend image (it ships via EAS, not
# a container) and is by far the largest subtree in this repo (RN/Expo
# node_modules, native build output) — never needed for the backend build.
app

# Build output recreated fresh inside the image; never trust the host's.
backend/dist
content/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests aren't part of the runtime image (harmless if compiled, but no reason
# to ship them or count them against build context size).
backend/test
content/test
voice-agent/tests

# content/ generation tooling and its non-generated artifacts: the backend
# image only needs content/generated + content/audio-out/manifest.json (see
# backend/Dockerfile), never the pipeline source, review exports, or the
# full (gitignored, mostly-absent-anyway) audio-out tree.
content/src
content/scripts
content/review-export
content/audio-out/*
!content/audio-out/manifest.json

# Editor / OS cruft, logs, local env files (never bake secrets into an image).
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
*.local
